  ($seed$ledgerline$seed$, $seed$Ledgerline$seed$, $seed$Reconciliation platform for a multi-entity finance team$seed$, $seed$Fintech · B2B SaaS$seed$, $seed$14 weeks + 4 weeks support$seed$, $seed$Full team · pod of 5$seed$, array[$seed$Backend$seed$, $seed$Database$seed$, $seed$Cloud$seed$, $seed$UI/UX$seed$]::text[], $seed$In this concept, a finance team of eight reconciles payouts from three banks and two payment processors across six legal entities — mostly in spreadsheets. Matching is manual, exceptions live in email threads, and there is no audit trail an external auditor would accept.$seed$, $seed$[{"title":"Data residency","text":"EU-only processing and storage"},{"title":"Auditability","text":"Every match and override must be explainable"},{"title":"No big-bang","text":"Run in parallel with spreadsheets for one close"},{"title":"Small team","text":"Two analysts own day-to-day operations"}]$seed$::jsonb, $seed$Event-driven matching service in Go, Postgres with partitioned ledgers, an exceptions queue designed with the analysts, and an audit trail from day one.$seed$, $seed$[{"name":"Month-end close","definition":"Days from period end to signed-off books"},{"name":"Auto-match rate","definition":"Share of transactions matched without review"},{"name":"Exception age","definition":"Median time an exception stays open"}]$seed$::jsonb, true, true, 'published'::public.publish_status),
